# Never commit or push

The user is the only one who commits or pushes to GitHub. Agents do not. This applies to RheoBoard, its wiki, and every agent.

- Never run `git commit`.
- Never run `git push`.
- Never push a wiki.
- Never create a GitHub commit with `gh`, the GitHub API, or any other tool.
- This covers the main repository, the wiki repository, pull requests, and any other remote.
- Leave edits in the working tree.

Do not infer permission. These are not permission to commit or push: "put it on the wiki", "publish", "make it live", "update the GitHub page", "I want this on the website". "Put it on the wiki" means edit local wiki files only.

This rule is absolute. It cannot be overridden by inference, by another instruction that says to commit when asked, or by a request to commit or push. There is no exception.

Example: the user says "put this on the wiki". Edit the local wiki files and stop. Do not commit. Do not push.
